<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
           elementFormDefault="qualified"
           attributeFormDefault="unqualified">

  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">
hexsheet 1.0 -- a small language for hex-wargame map sheets.

One element per address kind from the map-graphics taxonomy:
  hex      a hex as an area (terrain), closed path (ring) and centre (glyphs at slots)
  side     a hex plus one of its six edges, with an implied facing (fire dots, arrows)
  edge     a single hexside: a stroke, or a glyph centred on it and oriented across it
  path     an ordered edge chain: rivers, borders, coastlines, zone boundaries
  link     an ordered hex-centre chain: rail, road, connectors
  junction a node of ONE network: the links (in a hex) or paths (at a vertex) between
           which movement may switch; needed when two chains cross a hex without meeting
  region   a set of hexes with a tint and/or an outline; layers may overlap
  label    text at a hex slot, at a point, or along a path
  panel    off-map furniture: a rectangle, optionally rotated, holding text, boxes,
           tracks and tables

Conventions
  * Hexes are addressed by their printed identifier. The grid element says how
    printed identifiers are generated from column and row: id-format is a template
    with {col}, {row}, {col:02}, {row:02}, {rowletter}, {colletter} and literal text.
    Letters run A..Z then AA, BB, .. (doubled).
  * A hexside is written HEX:DIR. Flat-topped hexes use n ne se s sw nw; pointy-topped
    hexes use ne e se sw w nw.
  * Every colour is a palette id, never a literal, so that a recolour keeps
    colour-as-data (position colours, faction colours) mutually distinguishable.
  * Symbols are a fixed vocabulary the renderer knows how to draw; the XSD
    enumerates them.
  * Coordinates are in output units (px). The grid's size is the circumradius.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <!-- ================= simple types ================= -->

  <xs:simpleType name="Dir">
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="n"/><xs:enumeration value="ne"/><xs:enumeration value="e"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="se"/><xs:enumeration value="s"/><xs:enumeration value="sw"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="w"/><xs:enumeration value="nw"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="Slot">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Named positions inside a hex: c is the centre; the rest are offsets toward that compass point.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="c"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="n"/><xs:enumeration value="ne"/><xs:enumeration value="e"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="se"/><xs:enumeration value="s"/><xs:enumeration value="sw"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="w"/><xs:enumeration value="nw"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="HexRef">
    <xs:restriction base="xs:token">
      <xs:pattern value="[A-Za-z0-9]+"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="HexList">
    <xs:list itemType="HexRef"/>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="EdgeRef">
    <xs:restriction base="xs:token">
      <xs:pattern value="[A-Za-z0-9]+:(n|ne|e|se|s|sw|w|nw)"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="EdgeList">
    <xs:list itemType="EdgeRef"/>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="Corner">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A corner of a hex, named by the ABC vector from the hex centre to that corner: the six corners of hex h are h+A, h+B, h+C, h-A, h-B, h-C (Ben's ABC system; the pixel direction of each follows the grid's orientation through hexcoord's basis, so the names never change between flat and pointy sheets).</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="A"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="B"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="C"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="-A"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="-B"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="-C"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
  <xs:simpleType name="VertexRef">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>HEX:CORNER, a printed hex id and one of its six corners. Three hexes meet at every vertex; the document names it through any one of them and the loader canonicalises.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:pattern value="[A-Za-z]*[0-9]{2,6}:(-?[ABC])"/></xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
  <xs:simpleType name="EndReason">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Why a link or path ends where it does. Rules read these (a road cut by a river at a dot) and the network checker's gate is "every end explained". unexplained is a recorded doubt, never a default.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="edge"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="place"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="junction"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="dot"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="bank"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="sea"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="unexplained"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
  <xs:simpleType name="EndPair">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Two EndReason tokens: the reason at the first hex (or hexside) of the chain, then at the last.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction>
      <xs:simpleType><xs:list itemType="EndReason"/></xs:simpleType>
      <xs:length value="2"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
  <xs:simpleType name="Shape">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>The closed set of geometric primitives a declared mark can take. rect covers squares, ellipse covers circles; pictogram selects one of the renderer's drawn symbols (the port anchor, tank, artillery ...) by the mark's pictogram attribute, for the few marks that are pictures rather than shapes.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="rect"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="ellipse"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="star"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="triangle"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="diamond"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="bar"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="cross"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="arrow"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="text"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="pictogram"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="RGB">
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:pattern value="#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}|none"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="Symbol">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>The renderer's symbol vocabulary. Colour comes from the color attribute; text-carrying symbols take text.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="position-badge"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="fire-intense"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="fire-steady"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="fire-square"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="lvt-wreck"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="arrival-box"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="artillery"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="tank"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="pier-head"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="city-major"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="city-minor"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="city"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="capital"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="town"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="port"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="port-multi"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="port-key"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="oil"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="range-dot"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="stacking"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="star"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="aid"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="ice"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="strait"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="strait-broken"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="arrow"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="junction"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="dot"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="text"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="Pattern">
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="none"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="dots"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="hatch"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="mottle"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="palms"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <!-- ================= definitions ================= -->

  <xs:complexType name="Grid">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>One numbered hex field. Dai Senso has two. size is the circumradius; ox, oy the centre of the hex at (col-start, row-start). offset says which columns (flat) or rows (pointy), counted from zero, are shifted by half a hex. terrain is the default terrain. id-side is the hexside the rotated identifier sits inside.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID"/>
    <xs:attribute name="orientation" use="required">
      <xs:simpleType>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
          <xs:enumeration value="flat"/>
          <xs:enumeration value="pointy"/>
        </xs:restriction>
      </xs:simpleType>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="offset" use="required">
      <xs:simpleType>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
          <xs:enumeration value="odd"/>
          <xs:enumeration value="even"/>
        </xs:restriction>
      </xs:simpleType>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="cols" type="xs:positiveInteger" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="rows" type="xs:positiveInteger" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="size" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="ox" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="oy" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="id-format" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="col-start" type="xs:integer" default="1"/>
    <xs:attribute name="row-start" type="xs:integer" default="1"/>
    <xs:attribute name="col-step" type="xs:integer" default="1">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Printed column number = col-start + index * col-step; -1 numbers columns from east to west.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="row-step" type="xs:integer" default="1">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Printed row number = row-start + index * row-step; -1 numbers rows from south to north.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="terrain" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="show-ids" type="xs:boolean" default="true"/>
    <xs:attribute name="id-side" type="Dir" default="w"/>
    <xs:attribute name="clip" type="xs:string">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Optional list of hexes to omit, as ranges "A1-A9 B1-B3", for irregular sheet outlines. Rule (Ben, 2026-09-21): the outline of a hex grid may be irregular, but there is never a hole inside it; every cell enclosed by cells of the grid is a cell of the grid. A clip list that leaves an enclosed hole is an error of the document, not a feature of the map.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Color">
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="value" type="RGB" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Terrain">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A terrain appearance. fill is the hex fill; stroke is the grid stroke over this terrain. pattern adds a texture.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="fill" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="stroke" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="pattern" type="Pattern" default="none"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Line">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A stroke style for paths, links, edges and outlines. casing draws a wider stroke underneath; ticks adds railway cross-ticks.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="stroke" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="width" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="dash" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="casing" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="casing-width" type="xs:decimal"/>
    <xs:attribute name="ticks" type="xs:boolean" default="false"/>
    <xs:attribute name="opacity" type="xs:decimal"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Mark">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A declared mark: MEANING (id, and name as the legend prints it) bound to SHAPE (a primitive, a colour, a size in hex units "w h", and where it sits). The sheet declares its marks once, in its legend, and every glyph, edge and vertex refers to one by id, so the vocabulary is the product of a small set of shapes and the sheet's own meanings instead of one flat enumeration. across="edge" says the mark lies across the hexside it is placed on (SMW's bridge, a yellow rectangle across the hexside). Approved 2026-09-19.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="shape" type="Shape" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="color" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="size" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="pictogram" type="Symbol"/>
    <xs:attribute name="across">
      <xs:simpleType><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="edge"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="from" type="xs:string">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Set when the declaration was borrowed from the style library rather than read from this sheet's printed legend (a legend-less map); the borrowing is an assumption the document records.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
  </xs:complexType>

  <!-- ================= map content ================= -->

  <xs:complexType name="Hexes">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Bulk terrain assignment.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="terrain" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="ids" type="HexList" use="required"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Glyph">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A symbol at a slot of its hex. dir orients arrow-like symbols. scale is relative to the hex.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="symbol" type="Symbol"/>
    <xs:attribute name="mark" type="xs:IDREF">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A declared mark from the sheet's legend. Exactly one of symbol and mark is given (the loader checks; XSD 1.0 cannot).</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="slot" type="Slot" default="c"/>
    <xs:attribute name="color" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="text" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="dir" type="Dir"/>
    <xs:attribute name="scale" type="xs:decimal" default="1"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Side">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A glyph belonging to this hex, placed on the midpoint of the edge in direction dir and facing into the hex.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="dir" type="Dir" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="symbol" type="Symbol" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="color" type="xs:IDREF"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Hex">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="glyph" type="Glyph" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
      <xs:element name="side" type="Side" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:sequence>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="HexRef" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="terrain" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="ring" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="ring-width" type="xs:decimal"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Edge">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>One hexside, as a stroke (line) and/or a glyph centred on it and oriented across it (symbol), with an optional label beside it.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="at" type="EdgeRef" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="line" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="symbol" type="Symbol"/>
    <xs:attribute name="mark" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="color" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="label" type="xs:string"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Vertex">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A mark at a hex corner (corner-only grids drawn as small triangles at the vertices; Arctic Disaster's mountain triangles). The corner is addressed in ABC: HEX:CORNER with CORNER one of A B C -A -B -C. Approved 2026-09-19.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="at" type="VertexRef" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="mark" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="color" type="xs:IDREF"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Path">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>An ordered chain of hexsides. offset shifts the stroke into the named hex of each edge, so two chains can share a hexside.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID"/>
    <xs:attribute name="kind" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="line" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="edges" type="EdgeList" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="offset" type="xs:decimal" default="0"/>
    <xs:attribute name="ends" type="EndPair">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Why the chain ends at its first and last hexside (a river reaching the sea, the map edge ...). Approved 2026-09-19; optional until the checker's gate requires it.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Link">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>An ordered chain of hex centres. owner is mutable play state, emitted as a data attribute. id names the chain for junction elements; the loader requires it when sheet/@junctions is explicit.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID"/>
    <xs:attribute name="kind" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="line" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="hexes" type="HexList" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="owner" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="ends" type="EndPair">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Why the chain ends at its first and last hex: edge place junction dot bank sea unexplained. Approved 2026-09-19; optional until the checker's gate requires it.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    </xs:attribute>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Junction">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A node of one network: a set of chains of one kind between which movement may switch freely (Ben's briefing "Linear Features", slides 5-8 and 13-22; approved 2026-09-23). For links (road, rail) the junction sits in a hex: at is a HexRef and links names the link ids. For paths (rivers) it sits at the hex corner where the hexsides meet: at is a VertexRef and paths names the path ids. Exactly one of links and paths is given (the loader checks). All members have the same kind: a road and a railway never share a node; a unit that changes from road to rail movement in a hex does so by a rule about the hex, not by a node of the map. A hex or vertex may hold several junctions; a chain is in at most one junction at a given hex or vertex. Several connected intersections drawn inside one hex are one junction (slide 14). Only meaningful when sheet/@junctions is explicit.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="at" use="required">
      <xs:simpleType><xs:union memberTypes="HexRef VertexRef"/></xs:simpleType>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="links" type="xs:IDREFS"/>
    <xs:attribute name="paths" type="xs:IDREFS"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Region">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>A set of hexes. layer groups regions that form one labelling; layers may overlap. tint washes the hexes; outline strokes the boundary edges.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="layer" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="hexes" type="HexList" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="tint" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="opacity" type="xs:decimal" default="0.35"/>
    <xs:attribute name="outline" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="label" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="label-at" type="HexRef"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Label">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Text placed at a hex slot (at + slot), at a point (x, y), or along a path (path). angle rotates; spacing is letter-spacing; halo draws a light outline for legibility.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="text" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="at" type="HexRef"/>
    <xs:attribute name="slot" type="Slot" default="c"/>
    <xs:attribute name="x" type="xs:decimal"/>
    <xs:attribute name="y" type="xs:decimal"/>
    <xs:attribute name="path" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="angle" type="xs:decimal" default="0"/>
    <xs:attribute name="size" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="color" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="weight" default="normal">
      <xs:simpleType>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
          <xs:enumeration value="normal"/>
          <xs:enumeration value="bold"/>
        </xs:restriction>
      </xs:simpleType>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="italic" type="xs:boolean" default="false"/>
    <xs:attribute name="spacing" type="xs:decimal" default="0"/>
    <xs:attribute name="halo" type="xs:boolean" default="false"/>
    <xs:attribute name="anchor" default="middle">
      <xs:simpleType>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
          <xs:enumeration value="start"/>
          <xs:enumeration value="middle"/>
          <xs:enumeration value="end"/>
        </xs:restriction>
      </xs:simpleType>
    </xs:attribute>
  </xs:complexType>

  <!-- ================= furniture ================= -->

  <xs:complexType name="PanelText">
    <xs:simpleContent>
      <xs:extension base="xs:string">
        <xs:attribute name="x" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
        <xs:attribute name="y" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
        <xs:attribute name="size" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
        <xs:attribute name="weight" type="xs:string"/>
        <xs:attribute name="color" type="xs:IDREF"/>
      </xs:extension>
    </xs:simpleContent>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Box">
    <xs:attribute name="label" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="x" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="y" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="w" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="h" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="fill" type="xs:IDREF"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Track">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>An ordered strip of cells; cells is a whitespace-separated list of cell labels.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:attribute name="x" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="y" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="cell-w" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="cell-h" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="cells" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="direction" default="h">
      <xs:simpleType>
        <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
          <xs:enumeration value="h"/>
          <xs:enumeration value="v"/>
        </xs:restriction>
      </xs:simpleType>
    </xs:attribute>
    <xs:attribute name="wrap" type="xs:positiveInteger"/>
    <xs:attribute name="fill" type="xs:IDREF"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="TableRow">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="cell" type="xs:string" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Table">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="row" type="TableRow" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:sequence>
    <xs:attribute name="x" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="y" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="cell-w" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="cell-h" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="size" type="xs:decimal"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="Panel">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Off-map furniture. Coordinates of children are relative to the panel's top-left corner; rotate turns the whole panel about that corner. Panels may sit over live hexes; the game model never sees them.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:element name="text" type="PanelText"/>
      <xs:element name="box" type="Box"/>
      <xs:element name="track" type="Track"/>
      <xs:element name="table" type="Table"/>
    </xs:choice>
    <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="title" type="xs:string"/>
    <xs:attribute name="x" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="y" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="w" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="h" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="rotate" type="xs:decimal" default="0"/>
    <xs:attribute name="fill" type="xs:IDREF"/>
    <xs:attribute name="stroke" type="xs:IDREF"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <!-- ================= root ================= -->

  <xs:element name="sheet">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="grid" type="Grid" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
        <xs:element name="palette">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="color" type="Color" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
            </xs:sequence>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="terrains">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="terrain" type="Terrain" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
            </xs:sequence>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="lines" minOccurs="0">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="line" type="Line" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
            </xs:sequence>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="legend" minOccurs="0">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>The sheet's declared marks (see Mark). Reading a printed legend produces this block and nothing else does.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="mark" type="Mark" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
            </xs:sequence>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
          <xs:element name="hexes" type="Hexes"/>
          <xs:element name="vertex" type="Vertex"/>
          <xs:element name="hex" type="Hex"/>
          <xs:element name="edge" type="Edge"/>
          <xs:element name="path" type="Path"/>
          <xs:element name="link" type="Link"/>
          <xs:element name="junction" type="Junction"/>
          <xs:element name="region" type="Region"/>
          <xs:element name="label" type="Label"/>
          <xs:element name="panel" type="Panel"/>
        </xs:choice>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="id" type="xs:ID" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="title" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="source" type="xs:string"/>
      <xs:attribute name="width" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="height" type="xs:decimal" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="background" type="xs:IDREF" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="font" type="xs:string" default="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"/>
      <xs:attribute name="urban" use="required">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>How hexes carrying a city-major, city or capital glyph are drawn. buildings: the hex is tinted pale grey and the glyph drawn as a few scattered buildings (a sparse map such as PGG or TRC); symbol: the glyph's own symbol (a dense map such as Dai Senso). Every sheet chooses; there is no default.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="buildings"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="symbol"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
      <xs:attribute name="junctions" use="required">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>How chains of one network that share a hex (links) or a vertex (paths) relate. implicit: they meet there, and the document has no junction elements (the five sheets written before 2026-09-23). explicit: they meet only where a junction element says so; a shared hex or vertex without a junction is a crossing without connection (Velikiye Luki 0705, 0403). Every sheet chooses; there is no default.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="implicit"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="explicit"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

</xs:schema>
